                   is faithful, but the theorem rests on that validation.
                 · Mrl is held in hundredths and the share in whole percent;
                   upstream uses doubles, ceil(), and a tolerance comparison
                   that this core replaces with exact integer comparison. The
                   "unset" sentinel -1 is a Boolean flag. INT_MAX is the
                   subtype's last value. Counts are capped at 30000 so every
                   product in a contract stays in range.
                   EI_CountDonorsReachedDonorLimit is not modelled.

                 WHAT IS PROVED, graded. The two ceiling characterisations
                 carry the weight: the rounded-up ratio is exactly the least
                 count whose multiple by the donors reaches the recipients, and
                 likewise the scaled ceiling against one hundred. Then:
                 Donor_Limit is at least one, at least the fixed count when set,
                 and at least the scaled ceiling when a multiplier is set (these
                 follow from Integer'Max); when a multiplier of at least 1.00 IS
                 set, composing the last of those with Limit_Covers_Recipients
                 gives a limit of at least the rounded-up ratio, so the donors
                 together can cover every recipient at that cap — this holds only
                 when Has_M is true; and More_Respondents_Never_Hurt, which is
                 true because a share can never exceed one hundred percent.

